hey guys what's up I'm Alanna or char  Ilana Zod and welcome to my channel  today I'm going to be answering the most  common question that I get asked which  is how did I get a job at IGN it all  started in primary school to cut the  education part very short I just want to  wrap it all up by saying that I always  excelled in English I always wrote a lot  and I always wrote even in my spare time  this is something that I think is very  important to stress because I think  there are a lot of people who want to  work in games media or want to write for  IGN because they like games rather than  because they like writing I never want  to discourage anyone from trying to  learn a new skill or to improve in  something but if you don't like writing  and you only want to write about games  it might not be for you  you might want to consider all of the  other things that are to do in games  that you have maybe historically been  good at or are passionate about so after  graduating high school with relatively  good grades and a definite strong suit  in English I went on to study a Bachelor  of mass communication majoring in of  course journalism and entertainment to  backtrack a tiny bit I actually started  writing about games before I started  studying the way that I happened upon  that was basically I was looking for a  job just after graduating high school  and I found a listing on a website for a  volunteer games news write-up for a very  small website I started writing for that  website twice a week and I think I  worked there for six months or so I  don't remember but during the time that  I started writing for them I also  started writing for other websites as a  volunteer there were websites and  magazines that I found that I knew  because they were local and basically  what I started to do was compile  everything that I had written put it on  a separate website which I actually used  a tumblr blog and then I would reach out  to these websites on Facebook or Twitter  and say hey here's my work I'm really  passionate about this I would love to  write for you so I wrote for a bunch of  different websites completely for free  for I think around a year and I think  around the six months mark was where I  actually started to study at the same  time as well from there I started using  Twitter a lot more often I started  interacting with editors and community  managers on Twitter and trying to build  relationships whilst also sharing links  to every single thing that I wrote so  those people who I was getting to know  by a Twitter would also see all of my  work so I don't remember my timeline  perfectly but I did get to  point where I was using a casual job  that I was working on the weekends to  pay for my flights to go to events to  cover games in person and to meet other  people who worked in the industry I  found out about them by social media all  because I had asked community manages or  PR reps for their email addresses  I was absolutely zero dollars in my bank  account because everything I was doing  was being invested in this career and it  was at one of those events that I  actually got my first writing job I was  arguing with someone about why I like  taalib and he came up to me afterwards  and I think he said something like hey  I've seen some of your writing I thought  you were very articulate in that article  I want you to review games for us I will  pay you to do that I think this is  probably around the same point in time  where I started my youtube channel I  started my youtube channel as a way to  lend a video edit and to get more  comfortable on camera so it was  basically at the same time where I was  building up a video presence that he  eventually paid me to review games for  his website and things just kept kind of  going that way and that I used that to  pitch to other magazines or other  websites around that time was just after  I'd started making videos so I was  trying to get on video for more  companies so I was doing the same thing  that I did with writing full video is  basically contacting companies and  saying hey I want to make these videos  for you I think there are three separate  companies that have been relatively  heard of at this point that I was the  first one to make a news video for them  because I pitched them with it was also  around the same time that I was getting  a lot more comfortable in camera that I  started to pitch to radio stations and I  actually ended up getting a position on  a local radio station in Brisbane so I  was live on radio every Wednesday which  was awesome that's four triples edge  shot out to Zed games I love you guys  one of the things that I did in that  hustle was apply to a competition that  Xbox australiawow having to send someone  to e3 to be an Xbox insider I did not  win that competition I don't think I was  even a finalist in that competition but  it did mean that they knew who I was and  I think six months after that had  stopped being a thing I got a call from  someone who worked at Xbox Australia who  I guess had been keeping in the loop  with my writing in my videos and they  asked me to be the Xbox insider which  basically meant going  to events interviewing people and being  first impressions of games for xbox  australia's social channels so  everything was kind of coming together  and I was doing a lot of different  things and it was all in the interest of  we trying to get my name out there and  do things for free until I basically  felt like I had reached a point where I  had enough experience was confident  enough and was getting enough good  feedback that I kind of hit a point  where I was like I should be paid for  this so I'm pretty sure took two and a  half years until I got my first  full-time position at that point I  recognized that there was a ceiling in  Australia for the games industry  I used my degree to get me transferred  to the US as an international student  entirely with the goal of ending up at a  place like IGN and I applied for a job  in May of last year at IGN I had I think  three interviews it was like hours that  was one thing where I was interviewed by  like nearly 20 different people I think  in one day it was pretty crazy  but because I was still a student uh and  I was on a student visa the visa process  was really hard so I was technically  told that I had the job in May 2015  but I didn't actually start watching by  IGN until November 2015 because it took  that long for me to get a visa  it was rough and I'm pretty sure that  that covers everything I think so uh  it's hard to recount everything you've  done for the last five years but I  really hope that I haven't forgotten  anything Here I am going to disable  comments on this video but if you have  any more questions I will do my very  best to answer them as always there will  be links below to all my social channels  I do have to give a shout out to the two  people who supported my channel after  the last video which is Austin Foss and  Kyle Allen thank you guys so much this  is just absolutely amazing  YouTube is totally a thing that I do in  my spare time off the insane walk hours  so um I seriously just appreciate that  you guys appreciate that I guess  thank you guys so much I love you and  that is it for me today everyone I will  see you guys next time okay
 

